<title>CANADA: Prairie grainbelt faces slight frost risk Friday.</title>
<headline>Prairie grainbelt faces slight frost risk Friday.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairie grainbelt was forecast to see a slight risk of frost Friday morning, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>A moderate risk of frost was likely in northern Alberta's grainbelt Saturday and Sunday mornings, Environment Canada said in its 10-day frost outlook.</p>
<p>A moderate risk of frost was forecast for south Alberta's grainbelt Sunday with a slight risk for all of Saskatchewan and west Manitoba.</p>
<p>A high risk was seen on the entire grainbelt Oct 7.</p>
<p>A moderate risk of frost was forecast for Manitoba's grainbelt Oct 8.</p>
<p>Alberta's harvest was 50 percent complete, Saskatchewan's harvest was 53 percent done and Manitoba's harvest was about 75 percent done by Sept 30, provincial crop reports said.</p>
<p>The harvest had been delayed on the west Prairie due to rain and snow.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
